From: a52q UW agent <jarda.kotesovec@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:23:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] ipa: simple: Add lens shading correction (GPU debayer)

Static RGB gain mesh from the tuning file (grid + r/g/b tables, sensor
orientation, nodes spanning the frame), optionally faded out between two
analogue gains. The IPA passes the mesh through DebayerParams; the EGL
debayer uploads it once as an RGBA8 texture holding log2 gains and
multiplies the black-level-corrected RGB by the bilinearly sampled gain.
The CPU debayer ignores it.
